  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enabling Durable Solutions to Internal Displacement in Mozambique through a Joint Approach</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This joint programme will support the Mozambican Government to address durable solutions to internal displacement. The project has 3 components: (1) data for solutions, implemented through the creation of a multi-stakeholder forum with the national Government and UNCT members, strengthening existing data platforms that contain data related to SDGs indicators and more specifically data on durable solutions and IDPs, capacity building of relevant Government agencies and the implementation of joint data collection and analysis related to durable solutions for internally displaced persons. (2) community engagement, by carrying out robust quantitative and qualitative data collection on intentions and concerns of the affected population, convene a briefing and present findings from the data collection, as well as provide and share guidelines and recommendations to the Government and other stakeholders to perform inclusive and participatory community engagement mechanisms/approaches to set up durable solutions to displacement (3) On the policy advice component, the project plans to organize national seminars, thematic workshops, and advocacy campaigns and provide dedicated specialized expert advice to the Government to support the development and operationalization of existing Government policies. The project will be implemented by 4 agencies (IOM, UNFPA, UN-Habitat, and UNHCR).</narrative>
  </description>
